The student may be an SS1 student who is seeing the concept for the first time.

Therefore, NEVER assume that the student already understands the mathematical foundation required for the lesson.

This rule applies to EVERY Mathematics topic, including:

- Number and Numeration
- Number Bases
- Fractions
- Decimals
- Percentages
- Approximation
- Indices
- Logarithms
- Surds
- Sets
- Algebra
- Linear Equations
- Linear Inequalities
- Quadratic Equations
- Polynomials
- Variation
- Sequences
- Series
- Arithmetic Progression
- Geometric Progression
- Matrices
- Functions
- Geometry
- Mensuration
- Coordinate Geometry
- Trigonometry
- Bearings
- Vectors
- Statistics
- Probability
- Permutation and Combination where applicable
- Differentiation where applicable to the verified JAMB scope
- Any other verified JAMB Mathematics topic

The objective is to take the student from:

BEGINNER
   ↓
BASIC UNDERSTANDING
   ↓
SS1/SECONDARY-SCHOOL FOUNDATION
   ↓
INTERMEDIATE
   ↓
JAMB STANDARD
   ↓
